{
  name: "compliance"

  testpoints: [
    {
      name: rv32i
      desc: '''RV32I base integer instructions

            The 46 riscv-compliance rv32i tests (riscv-test-suite/rv32i), run on the Xcelium
            compliance testbench with cheriot_enable_i low and high. Each test's signature must
            match the suite's reference output exactly; a missing signature is a failure. The
            enable-high run checks that plain RISC-V code behaves the same with CHERIoT enabled.

            Expected failures (counted as expected while they fail, reported XPASS if they pass):

            - I-MISALIGN_JMP-01 (enable_low, enable_high): misa is read-only, so C cannot be
              disabled and a 2-byte-aligned jump target is legal; the test expects an
              instruction-address-misaligned exception
            - I-MISALIGN_LDST-01 (enable_low, enable_high): misaligned loads and stores are
              handled in hardware; the test expects an address-misaligned exception

            Not in this testplan:

            - I-ECALL-01: trap handler installed with csrw mtvec: 256-byte mtvec truncation
              (CHERIoT off), legacy mtvec not the trap vector (CHERIoT on)
            - I-EBREAK-01: as I-ECALL-01'''
      stage: V1
      tags: ["enable_low", "enable_high"]
      tests: ["rv32i_I-ADD-01", "rv32i_I-ADDI-01", "rv32i_I-AND-01", "rv32i_I-ANDI-01",
              "rv32i_I-AUIPC-01", "rv32i_I-BEQ-01", "rv32i_I-BGE-01", "rv32i_I-BGEU-01",
